   "plain": "Three papers decide a lot in El Ocotillo. **Title** decides whether a house is legally the family's, which decides whether a bank will lend against it or an insurer will cover it. The **DNI** (national ID card) is needed for a passport, a formal job, a bank account and most public services. A **U.S. visa** decides whether the road north can be taken legally; for most families here it cannot. Birth registration, often the first paper problem elsewhere, is not the main one here: almost every child is registered.",
