   "plain": "To fix a roof after the rains, rebuild after a fire, or stock a *pulpería* (corner store), a family needs a few thousand lempiras at once. Banks lend most cheaply to people with documented income and title. Microfinance lends to small earners at about a third of the loan a year. A daily street lender (*gota a gota*, drip by drip) asks for nothing up front and collects every day, with threats if a payment is late.",
