  {
   "h": "Handle with care (adults first)",
   "items": [
    "Gangs, extortion, deportation and violence are present in families students meet. **Never ask a family about them.** These questions go to IS staff.",
    "Do not use stories of violence or deportation to make the trip feel serious or brave.",
    "Follow IS's security rules without turning them into a story about danger.",
    "Never ask a family about its title, its papers, its lenders or whether it pays extortion. These are questions for IS staff."
   ]
  },
  {
   "h": "Framings that would be disrespectful or turn the trip into poverty tourism",
   "items": [
    "Children of the dump / families who live in garbage — the people are a community with a name; the dump is a city decision next to them.",
    "Asking families to explain their poverty, their migration or their safety.",
    "they have so little but they are so happy (romanticizing) and why don't they just… (blaming).",
    "Using donor language (rescue, transform, lives in trash) as if it were the community's own description.",
    "The structure decides everything — it erases the scholars, mothers and staff working on the door."
   ]
  }
